          },
          "code": "ASSIGN_VARIABLE_NON_UI_FLOW",
          "id": "1772043879382",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778277299050",
              "name": "TestResult",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.TestResult}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1772043910848",
              "name": "EffectiveDateVar",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EffectiveDate}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1772043899758",
              "name": "OrganizationIdVar",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OrganizationId}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1772043888419",
              "name": "InventoryItemIdVar",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.InventoryItemId}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "whether the model test is done",
            "name": "Is Test Done"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "false": "1770329618116",
            "true": "1778525782283"
          },
          "code": "IS_TEST_DONE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1778273565662",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778273565662_condition",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.TestResult != null && $context.$variables.TestResult != \"\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_ORDERMANAG_DIAGNOSERULES",
            "functionName": "autoModelTestWAllRuleFilter",
            "name": "callAutoModelTestWAllRuleFilter"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778259531260"
          },
          "code": "CALLAUTOMODELTESTWALLRULEFILTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1778087130377",
          "id": "1770329618116",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773767841482_1",
              "name": "InventoryItemId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.InventoryItemIdVar}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1773767841483_2",
              "name": "OrganizationId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.OrganizationIdVar}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1773767841483_3",
              "name": "EffectiveDate",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.EffectiveDateVar}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Identify Node Path"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778600049406"
          },
          "code": "IDENTIFY_NODE_PATH",
          "id": "1778525782283",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778525782284_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Identify a node path String using the user message {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and the test result {{$context.$variables.TestResult}}, and assign it to nodePath in output.\n\nThe test result has a \"nodesWithConflicts\" section with zero to multiple entries. Each entry has a node name and a node path.\n\n1. If this section is empty, set nodePath to \"noop\".\n2. If this section contains exactly one entry: In this case the user message is in response to whether they want you to further analyze an item. If the user message is \"no\", or similarly, sounds like they don't want to proceed, set nodePath to \"noop\". If the user message sounds like they agree to proceed, copy the exact node path String in the entry to nodePath. Otherwise, if the user message sounds irrelevant to whether they want to proceed or not, set nodePath to \"noop\".\n3. Otherwise this section contains multiple entries\n3a. If the user message seems to mention the name of an item, try to match the item name to a node name in the entries. If a close match is found, copy the exact corresponding node path String to nodePath. If no close match is found, set nodePath to \"again\".\n3b. If the user message mentions the position of an item such as \"the first item\", \"second item\", \"last item\", find the entry according to the specified position (such as the 1st entry, the 2nd entry, the last entry accordingly). If such an entry is found, copy the exact corresponding node path String to nodePath. If not, set nodePath to \"again\".\n3c. Otherwise set nodePath to \"again\"."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"nodePath\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n        \"nodePath\"\n    ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Assign Test Result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779308494509"
          },
          "code": "ASSIGN_TEST_RESULT",
          "id": "1778259531260",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778259542323",
              "name": "TestResult",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CALLAUTOMODELTESTWALLRULEFILTER.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "If Debug"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1778601854602",
            "false": "1778275956045"
          },
          "code": "IF_DEBUG",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1778600049406",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778600049407_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{false}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ProcessResponse"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PROCESSRESPONSE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1778087130377",
          "id": "1770329703071",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770329703071_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "First tell the user \"The rules test was performed at [time].\" where [time] is {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}} in \"HH:mm:ss\" format (omit the date and only report the time). Now start a new paragraph in your response.\n\nNow look into the following Json output:\n{{$context.$nodes.CALLAUTOMODELTESTWALLRULEFILTER.$output}}\n\nIt contains a \"nodesWithConflicts\" section. If the \"nodesWithConflicts\" section is empty, tell the user \"The model has passed the automated rules test with no issues detected. You may close the chat window now.\" and you are done.\n\nIf the \"nodesWithConflicts\" section is not empty, tell the user \"The following issues are found:\". Then start a new paragraph in your response.\n\nThe \"nodesWithConflicts\" section is a Json array. Do the following for each entry:\n1. Start a new paragraph by saying \"Item [node name] cannot be selected. Here are the relevant rules that it participates in:\". \n2. For each entry in the \"rule map\" array, report the \"rules\" array as a bullet list sorted alphabetically. Note that the \"rules\" have an associated \"model\". If the model is \"root\" we are fine. But if the model is not \"root\", report each rule with additional text \" - from referenced model [model]\".\n\nIf there is only a single node reported above, tell the user \"I can further analyze why this item cannot be selected, and suggest how to fix it. It may take a minute or two. Would you like me to do that?\". Otherwise, tell the user \"I can further analyze why each item cannot be selected, and suggest how to fix it. It may take a minute or two. Just tell me which item you would like me to analyze.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "If Node Found"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1778278534410",
            "false": "1778600430504"
          },
          "code": "IF_NODE_FOUND",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1778275956045",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778275956048_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFY_NODE_PATH.$output.nodePath != \"noop\" && $context.$nodes.IDENTIFY_NODE_PATH.$output.nodePath != \"again\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Print Debug Info"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "PRINT_DEBUG_INFO",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1778275956045",
          "id": "1778601854602",
          "inputs": [
